## What it is

xBloom has been making automatic pour-over machines since 2022, which makes it the "OG" of the category. The Studio is the current model, and it does everything in one box.

- **Grinder:** built in, 48mm stainless conical burrs with 80 settings. You can also use it on its own for French press or Chemex.
- **Scale:** built in, reads to 0.1g
- **Brewer:** you set the temperature, water volume, bloom, pour speed and pour pattern (straight, spiral and others), with pauses between pours
- **App:** shows a live brew graph and has a library of recipes other users have shared
- **Capacity:** a single cup (about 12oz) at a time

It has three modes. **Autopilot** brews xBloom's pre-portioned xPods. **Copilot** runs your own beans with a saved recipe. **Freesolo** gives you direct control of the grinder, brewer and scale.

## In the video

In [One Of These Coffee Robots Just Beat Keurig](https://youtu.be/En-YPVqqr6k), Daddy Got Coffee puts it up against the Cosori Juni and Breville Spiral Luxe. It's the most customizable of the three, mostly because of the full-featured app.

## Who it's for

Tinkerers who want to dial in every variable and save recipes for each bag. If you'd rather press one button and walk away, the [Breville Spiral Luxe](/coffee/products/breville-spiral-luxe) is simpler.
